maya: quick Q — planning a small canary to switch inference-gateway from ALB TLS termination -> TLS passthrough for customer-x (moving to NLB passthrough). Terraform plan looks ok but two things I'm worried about:
1) K8s Service probe binding: our pod listen port is 9090, healthcheck currently hits 8080. Will the LB healthcheck fail if Service.targetPort != probe port?
2) Gateway API SecretBinding: cert lives in 'platform-certs' ns, Gateway in 'inference' ns — can we reference cross-namespace secrets or do we need to copy cert into inference ns?

Plan snippet I'm iterating on:
```hcl
resource "kubernetes_service" "inference-gw" {
  metadata {
    name = "inference-gw"
    annotations = {
      "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-type" = "nlb"
      "service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-backend-protocol" = "ssl"
    }
  }
  spec {
    type = "NodePort"
    ports {
      name = "tls"
      port = 443
      target_port = 9090
      protocol = "TCP"
    }
  }
}
```

Anyone spot a missing piece? cc @sam @jules
